      "writtenOn": "2020-01-30T22:52:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You bail for current \u003d\u003d 0 at 402, change the logic @ 402 to have this executed.\n\nBatteryStatus \u003d CHARGING while connected with 0 average current is a failure: it might be OK if tested with instant current (yet testing battery status against average current has too many pitfalls)\n\nCHARGING while not connected is a failure",
      "revId": "98a3e115fadb627b2a4e65883d1a50df480baad9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d20cb6bc_f228d996",
        "filename": "health/2.0/vts/functional/VtsHalHealthV2_0TargetTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 424,
      "author": {
        "id": 1319951
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-30T22:52:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003d NOT_CHARGING with 0 current is OK\n\u003d DISCHARGING with current \u003e 0 is a failure.\n\u003d DISCHARGING with 0 average current is not a failure unless the condition persists over time\n\nDISCHARGING with 0 current is possible right after disconnect when you compare state to average . It is possible (but unlikely) to have DISCHARGING with 0 instantaneous current since \"instantaneous\" is usually averaged over a (very short) period of time.\n\nNOTE: reporting NOT_CHARGING while disconnected is a failure",
      "revId": "98a3e115fadb627b2a4e65883d1a50df480baad9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d97f59b3_72fef449",
        "filename": "health/2.0/vts/functional/VtsHalHealthV2_0TargetTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 517,
