        "id": 1319951
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-30T22:52:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instantaneous current might (briefly) invert the sign when reacting to transient loads since the behavior depends mostly on the averaging window used by the fuel gauge (yes, instantaneous current is averaged over some period).\n\nAdding a test on it might cause more problems that it tries to solve: this should not be a failure (same remark later)",
      "revId": "98a3e115fadb627b2a4e65883d1a50df480baad9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b474aef_73245e2d",
        "filename": "health/2.0/vts/functional/VtsHalHealthV2_0TargetTest.cpp",
